{{en-adj|head=[[cold]] [[short]]|?}}
cold shortness is happens in steel due to high P contain. when %p increases than in cold working Fe3p compound accumulate on grain boundaries. due to this steel high energy level grain boundaries became less energy and behave as brittle material. when working temperature became low than it became low energy so in less strength shows at grain boundaries. this is called cold shortness. due to cold shortness brittle properties increased and cracks developed. 
# {{metallurgy}} Of metal which is brittle at low temperatures.

